[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_page")
id = &"fighting"
title = "Fighting"
summary = "Only the men in contact fight, so shape and facing decide the battle."
body = "Only the men in CONTACT fight. A squad deals damage in proportion to how many
of its soldiers are actually within reach of an enemy soldier — so the shape
of a squad decides how much of it is in the battle at all.

That makes frontage real. A wide line meets more of the enemy than a deep
column of the same troops, and beats it. It also makes envelopment ordinary
geometry rather than a special rule: come round a flank and more of your men
are touching than of theirs.

## Where a blow lands

A hit from the flank costs {Combat.FLANK_MORALE_MULT} times the morale a
frontal one does; from the rear, {Combat.REAR_MORALE_MULT} times. Your squads
have a FACING and you can order it — dragging with the right button draws a
line and faces it. Bracing a line is a defence. Getting behind somebody is an
attack.

Formations change what a squad SUFFERS from each direction, how much it takes
from arrows, and how fast it walks. The numbers are on the Formations page.

## Charging

A charge is an attack-move at {SquadSim.CHARGE_SPEED_MULT} times speed, with a
single blow at {Combat.CHARGE_IMPACT_MULT} times damage waiting at the end —
and the charge is SPENT on that blow. Ordering a charge into something already in contact just
gives you an attack-move, so there is no free impact for clicking again.

Tired troops cannot charge. Below {SquadSim.CHARGE_MIN_FATIGUE} stamina a
charge is refused, and a charge already running ends at
{SquadSim.CHARGE_EXHAUST_FLOOR}. Sprinting, running and fighting drain
stamina; standing still restores it. Charge, rest, charge has a price.

## Across a shoreline

Melee does not cross a shoreline, in EITHER direction. Your soldiers
cannot reach a ship, and a ship cannot reach the shore. Missiles cross
it freely.

That is what makes a beach dangerous: an army caught on one by a warship
is shot at and cannot answer, unless it brought archers.

The rule is deliberately not the same as a wall's, which stops melee only
ONE way — you cannot strike a man on a wall from the ground, and he can
strike you.

## Ground

Attacking downhill multiplies your damage by {Combat.DOWNHILL_MULT}, uphill
by {Combat.UPHILL_MULT}. Take the high ground.

## Research

Research changes what your troops are made of. A tech that raises damage,
health or reach applies to every squad you own — including the ones already
standing in the field, not only the next ones you train. You can see your own
lines and your allies'; what an enemy has researched is hidden, so a squad
that hits harder than you expected may simply be a better-researched one.

## Standing orders

A stance is a rule a squad keeps following without being told again.

- GUARD holds position instead of chasing something that wanders past.
- SKIRMISH backs a missile squad away from anything closing on it.
- HOLD FIRE waits until you explicitly order an attack.
- RUN moves faster and spends stamina to do it."
sources = Array[String](["res://combat.gd", "res://squad_sim.gd", "res://decisions/D-20260819-only-men-in-contact-fight.md", "res://decisions/D-20260819-a-charge-is-spent-on-its-impact.md", "res://decisions/D-20260819-tired-men-fight-uphill.md", "res://decisions/D-20260819-stances-are-standing-orders.md"])
stamp = "0dccee2465eccf913059c37427415ce168dd3e25a152403ae469bcf8a4027789"
